print(p1("()()")))  # Should return False
print(p1("((()))"))  # Should return True
print(p1("((())))"))  # Should return False
```
This implementation uses a simple loop to count the number of opening and closing parentheses. If the number of opening parentheses is equal to the number of closing parentheses at the end of the loop, the parentheses are balanced, and the function returns `True`. Otherwise, it returns `False`.

