In Model-View-Presenter (MVP) design, the presenter is responsible for handling the application's logic and updating the view with the help of the model. Here's a simple "Hello World" example in Python using the MVP design pattern:
```python
class HelloWorldModel:
    def __init__(self):
        self.message = "Hello, World!"

class HelloWorldView(object):
    def display(self, message):
        print(message)

class HelloWorldPresenter(object):
    def __init__(self, model, view):
        self.model = model
        self.view = view

    def update(self):
        self.view.display(self.model.message)

# Usage example
model = HelloWorldModel()
view = HelloWorldView()
presenter = HelloWorldPresenter(model, view)
presenter.update()
```
