In this modified version of the function, the base case is `n <= 1`, which means that the function will return the input value `n` if it is less than or equal to 1. This will stop the recursion and prevent the error message from being generated.

Alternatively, you can set a maximum recursion depth using the `sys.setrecursionlimit()` function to limit the number of recursive calls that can be made. For example:
